# Research brief

## Objective (verbatim, experiment-repo issue #1)

> Estimate π by Monte Carlo sampling.
>
> Draw 1,000,000 points uniformly in the unit square, count those inside the quarter circle of radius 1, and take 4 × (inside / total) as the estimate. Repeat with 20 independent seeds and report the mean estimate with a 95% confidence interval across the seeds, and its error against math.pi.
>
> Report: `report/report.md`, half a page: the estimate, the interval, the error and how many points were drawn in all.

## Supplied material and interpretation

The objective issue is the complete supplied material. There are no supplied data files or related papers. The required data are newly generated independent uniform pairs (x,y) in [0,1)². A point is inside when x²+y² ≤ 1. Each seed contributes one estimate, 4 times its inside count divided by 1,000,000. The study requires 20 such estimates and 20,000,000 total points.

Use a two-sided Student t interval for the mean of the 20 seed estimates: mean ± t(0.975,19) × sample standard deviation / sqrt(20). This estimates Monte Carlo uncertainty in the average across independent random streams. Report signed and absolute error relative to Python math.pi, clearly labelled. Record the RNG, seed construction, per-seed counts, versions and reproducible code as supporting working material. No plots or external comparisons are required; a concise numerical report fits the requested half page.

## Ownership proposal

experiment-repo owns random sampling, analysis, checks and numerical evidence. paper-repo owns the final half-page report and its formatting. internal-review-repo independently checks the analysis and final report and handles approval. No feasibility gap is apparent at this scale.
